                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I played this years ago for quie a long time, the 3k hours is obviously inflated by being forced to be online while doing afk activities, but I still put a ton of hours, and ultimately money into this game during the time I played. Roughly 500 dollars over the course of a few years. \n\nThen circumstances changed for me and I wasn't gaming for a few years. Recently I was looking at Crimson Desert and the upcoming DLC and I thought man, I should check out BDO again. So I downloaded the game, which I've always played through steam and actually quite excitedly logged in.\n\nI was asked for my name and E-Mail which fine a little confused since it's through steam I thought, I had been recieving E-Mails to my primary account from them over the years so I didn't really think anything of it, filled it out and clicked connect. \n\nMy account is gone, all that time, all that money everything, gone. I have had a steam account for 20+years and everygame on my steam account that I've played in those 20 years still have my account regardless of my time away from any respective title, but PA just deleted my account? I tried going through support but it doesn't want payment details, it doesn't want steam account details or E-Mail or anything one would naturally assume you'd need to find an old account, no it wants my Family name? A name that wasn't even my primary charcters name? none of which unfortunatenly I can remember.\n\nSo that's it, years and money gone because why? No clue. I have an Everquest account that has survived 25 years of changing company hands all tied to the original e-mail and always there, but this game, deletes me after a 3 year absence? I was really interested in Crimson Desert and was excited to revisit this title before buying that game and the DLC but no longer. Now I guess I not only will I not be playing BDO but I will also never touch another product from Pearl Abyss for the rest of my life.\n\nI am absolutely incensed at the level of disrespect for my time and my money that this company has displayed toward me and infuriated that I have absolutely zero recourse in terms of getting any of that time or money back.",
